    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Step 1 · read request\nChecks its input, reads the system prompt and the step 1 contract from `shared/`, and asks Ollama (`POST /api/chat`, the contract as `format`, temperature 0, seed 42). `app.step1_read_answer` checks the answer against the contract and the request. A bad answer is sent back once with its errors; a second bad answer stops this workflow with `step 1 answer failed twice`. A good answer is checked against the output contract again and returned with `llm` (model, tries, tokens, ms). Writes nothing: the pipeline logs and saves.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "23b8799d-fa00-488c-ba94-5006e4aaeb83",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4b5752a3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -96,
        -224
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "81c10a7c-2b40-4815-a435-226473f267c3",
      "name": "Test data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Test data · editor run\nPin this on `When Executed by Another Workflow` (open the node, use the output panel's edit / mock-data control, paste the JSON, save), then click *Execute workflow*.\nCalls the model for real. Writes nothing (`run_id: 0` belongs to no run).\n\n```json\n[{\"run_id\": 0, \"request\": \"I want a classic West Coast IPA that is properly bitter. Make it 20 litres at about 6.5 % ABV.\", \"model\": \"hf.co/unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF:UD-Q6_K\", \"think\": false}]\n```",
        "color": 5,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 340
      }
    },
